The issue with the previous test was that when the vulnerability didn't exist (i.e., the function reverted on invalid inputs), it called `fail()` which forced a test failure. This caused tests to incorrectly fail when contracts were secure. The fix removes the `fail()` calls and uses assertions only to verify vulnerabilities exist.

Here's the corrected test script:

